  "content": {
    "id": "v2-03df2-p64-practice-slot-11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A triangle is formed by the $x$-axis and the two given lines. Find, correct to the nearest degree, the three angles of the triangle.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-03df2-p64-practice-slot-11-slot-11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=\\sqrt3x$ and $y=-\\sqrt3x+6\\sqrt3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$60^\\circ$, $60^\\circ$, $60^\\circ$",
          "worked": "For $y=\\sqrt3x$: $\\tan\\theta_1=\\sqrt3$, so $\\theta_1=60^\\circ$.\nFor $y=-\\sqrt3x+6\\sqrt3$: $\\tan\\theta_2=-\\sqrt3$, so $\\theta_2=\\tan^{-1}(-\\sqrt3)+180^\\circ=120^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Angle at the origin}&=60^\\circ\\\\\\text{Angle at the }x\\text{-intercept}&=180^\\circ-120^\\circ=60^\\circ\\\\\\text{Third angle}&=180^\\circ-60^\\circ-60^\\circ=60^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-03df2-p64-practice-slot-11-slot-11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=2x$ and $x+y=9$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$63^\\circ$, $45^\\circ$, $72^\\circ$",
          "worked": "For $y=2x$: $\\tan\\theta_1=2$, so $\\theta_1=\\tan^{-1}(2)\\approx63^\\circ$.\nFor $x+y=9$: $y=-x+9$, so $\\tan\\theta_2=-1$ and $\\theta_2=\\tan^{-1}(-1)+180^\\circ=135^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Angle at the origin}&\\approx63^\\circ\\\\\\text{Angle at the }x\\text{-intercept}&=180^\\circ-135^\\circ=45^\\circ\\\\\\text{Third angle}&\\approx180^\\circ-63^\\circ-45^\\circ=72^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      }
    ]
  },
